cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use serbiaciv in research, teaching or journalism, please cite it as below. Cite the underlying datasets (RZS, Eurostat, Copernicus, ESA WorldCover, OpenStreetMap and others) as their publishers require."
title: "serbiaciv: Serbia as a strategy-game map, built from real data"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aleksandar
    family-names: Ilic
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/acailic/serbiaciv"
url: "https://acailic.github.io/serbiaciv/"
abstract: >-
  An interactive hexagonal map of Serbia drawn like a 4X strategy game,
  combining public geographic and statistical data (2022 census, RZS,
  Eurostat, Copernicus DEM, ESA WorldCover, OpenStreetMap) with city views,
  resources and thematic lenses. Interface in Serbian Latin and Cyrillic.
keywords:
  - Serbia
  - open data
  - data visualization
  - interactive map
  - census
  - hexagonal grid
references:
  - type: software
    title: usaciv
    authors:
      - given-names: Andrej
        family-names: Karpathy
    url: "https://karpathy.ai/usaciv"
    license: MIT
